  "recipeCuisine": "Italy",
  "name": "Bolognese Sauce",
  "text": "Bolognese Sauce\n\nPreparation time: 15 minutes\n\nCooking time: 75 minutes\n\nYield: 6\n\nIngredients\n\n25 g (1 oz) butter,\n\n2 tbsp olive oil,\n\n1 onion (finely chopped),\n\n2 celery sticks (finely chopped),\n\n2 cloves of garlic (crushed),\n\n500 g (1 lb) lean minced beef,\n\n200 g (7 oz) spicy Italian sausage (skinned),\n\n300 ml (1/2 pint) red or white wine,\n\n400 g (13  oz) can of chopped tomatoes,\n\n1 tsp caster sugar,\n\n2 bay leaves,\n\n1 tsp dried oregano,\n\n2 tbsp  sun dried tomato paste,\n\nsalt and pepper.\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Melt the butter with the oil in a large heavy based saucepan and gently fry the onion and celery for 5 minutes.\n\n2. Add the garlic, beef and the skinned sausage, and cook until they are lightly coloured, breaking up the mince and sausage with a wooden spoon.\n\n3. Add the wine and allow it to bubble for 2 minutes until slightly evaporated. Add the tomatoes, sugar, bay leaves, oregano, tomato paste, and a little salt and pepper, and bring to the boil. Reduce the heat to it’s lowest setting, cover the pan with a lid and cook for 1 hour, stirring occasionally, until thick and pulpy.",
  "prepTime": "PT15M",
  "cookTime": "PT1H15M",
  "recipeYield": "6",
  "recipeIngredient": [
    "25 g (1 oz) butter,",
    "2 tbsp olive oil,",
    "1 onion (finely chopped),",
    "2 celery sticks (finely chopped),",
    "2 cloves of garlic (crushed),",
    "500 g (1 lb) lean minced beef,",
    "200 g (7 oz) spicy Italian sausage (skinned),",
    "300 ml (1/2 pint) red or white wine,",
    "400 g (13  oz) can of chopped tomatoes,",
    "1 tsp caster sugar,",
    "2 bay leaves,",
    "1 tsp dried oregano,",
    "2 tbsp  sun dried tomato paste,",
    "salt and pepper."
  ],
  "recipeInstructions": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "Melt the butter with the oil in a large heavy based saucepan and gently fry the onion and celery for 5 minutes."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "Add the garlic, beef and the skinned sausage, and cook until they are lightly coloured, breaking up the mince and sausage with a wooden spoon."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "Add the wine and allow it to bubble for 2 minutes until slightly evaporated. Add the tomatoes, sugar, bay leaves, oregano, tomato paste, and a little salt and pepper, and bring to the boil. Reduce the heat to it’s lowest setting, cover the pan with a lid and cook for 1 hour, stirring occasionally, until thick and pulpy."
